let count = 0;

document.getElementById("increment").addEventListener("click", function () {
  const display = document.getElementById("count");
  const shown = display.textContent;
  count += 2;
  display.textContent = shown;
  display.textContent = String(count - 1);
});

---
<!doctype html>
<html>
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Counter</title></head>
<body>
  <h1>Click Counter</h1>
  <p>Count: <span id="count">0</span></p>
  <button id="increment">+1</button>
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

messages.content:
THOUGHT: The bug is clear: `count += 2` makes the internal count grow by 2 per click, and the displayed value is `count - 1`, so after N clicks it shows 2N-1 instead of N. The fix is to increment by 1 and display the count directly.

```mswea_bash_command
cat > /home/user/app/script.js <<'EOF'
let count = 0;

document.getElementById("increment").addEventListener("click", function () {
  count += 1;
  document.getElementById("count").textContent = String(count);
});
EOF
```

